{"id": "EUVD-2026-102503", "enisaUuid": "5e69ae6f-263c-3c0e-ae61-76889ef5d626", "description": "BISHENG through 3.0.0-beta4 contains an insecure direct object reference vulnerability that allows authenticated low-privileged users to read other users' parsed documents by supplying arbitrary file_id values. Attackers can enumerate sequential file ids against GET /api/v1/knowledge/file_bbox to retrieve extracted page text from other users' and tenants' knowledge bases.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T21:43:47", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T14:19:20", "baseScore": 7.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@hieuPenguinnn/bisheng-knowledge-file-bbox-cross-user-idor", "https://github.com/dataelement/bisheng/blob/v3.0.0-beta4/src/backend/bisheng/knowledge/api/endpoints/knowledge.py#L663-L670", "https://github.com/dataelement/bisheng/blob/v3.0.0-beta4/src/backend/bisheng/knowledge/domain/services/knowledge_service.py#L2523-L2533", "https://github.com/dataelement/bisheng", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/bisheng-through-3.0.0-beta4-idor-via-api-v1-knowledge-file-bbox"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111363", "GHSA-37gw-p3c6-34pr"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "841d5d46-deac-3173-a38e-cc7a1d5e6156", "product": {"name": "bisheng", "vendor": {"name": "dataelement"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.0.0-beta4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "a5a7448b-5e22-3c2c-b799-220618bf766e", "vendor": {"name": "dataelement"}}], "isExploited": false}